2026-10-30 23:55 Findings before code: (1) a nested do_task forks a child that opens its own connection and exits 0 — its return value and package state never reach the caller (verified with a local toy Rexfile under Rex 1.16.1: do_task returned the Rex::Task object, X unset; a dying child is logged as ERROR and makes rex exit 1, but the parent carries on). So the gfx target cannot come back from detect_gpu while _maybe_detect_gpu calls it through do_task. (2) Rex registers every task as a function too; called that way it runs in-process on the current connection, returns the task's value and propagates die (verified, same pid). Plan: detect_gpu and install_amd are called as task functions (still tasks with callers, t/196 holds), install_amd returns the ocp.internal/amd-gpu.gfx-target label(s), _install_agent/_install_server add them to node_labels before install_agent/install_server. Preflight reads no node_labels (Rex::Rancher docs: labels read only at registration), so adding them after the preflight changes nothing it checks. install_nvidia stays a forked do_task, unchanged. (3) DRA init image: the pinned rocm/k8s-gpu-dra-driver:v1.0.1 (UBI 9 minimal) has sh=bash and sleep, and runs upstream's wait loop (docker run, 2026-10-31) — reuse it, no new pin. (4) All four AMD tags exist on Docker Hub, amd64 only (hub API 2026-10-31).

