2026-10-31 00:18 Also found (for other lanes; I changed none of it):
(1) apply lane, must land with this commit: the three new Versions keys are refused by ocp update until lib/OCP/Cmd/Update.pm %APPLIED_BY_APPLY lists amd_device_plugin, amd_dra_driver and amd_metrics_exporter (probably with the gpu_enabled skip the NVIDIA ones have). t/94 'every manifest component has a known outcome' and both '--force ... runs end to end' subtests are red until then (checked on host).
(2) provider + apply lanes: OCP::Rex::install_server/install_agent build an explicit param list and drop gpu_amd_integrated, and Apply::Bootstrap does not pass it. The OCP::Node path (node add/robocop, run_task with %params) carries it through. So only cluster-wide gpu.amd.integrated: true misses the bootstrap control plane; its iGPU keeps the default (left alone), which is the safe side.
(3) apply/k251: labels go in via config.yaml node-label, which the kubelet reads only at registration. A node already joined before k249 does not get the marker or the gfx label from a re-run install, and the changed config.yaml restarts its rke2/k3s service once (Rex::Rancher restarts on a config change). Such nodes need a rejoin or the after-join Node patch.
(4) Behaviour change, by design: under gpu.driver operator, Rex::GPU::Detect::Sysfs now runs, so a host whose sysfs cannot be read dies there, where operator mode used to skip detection.
(5) Assumption on rex-gpu k1: verify_amd(gpus => [...]) reports only the GPUs it is given. If it reports every KFD node, a skipped iGPU's gfx target would end up in the gfx labels.

